// A schedule can run a schedule that was declared before it: that one's
// runs take their place in it, with its parameters the values given. So a
// module can offer the steps it needs in their order as one.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/schedules.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s

// CHECK:      say 0
// CHECK-NEXT: add 10: 10
// CHECK-NEXT: say 10
// CHECK-NEXT: add 5: 15
// CHECK-NEXT: say 15
// CHECK-NEXT: add 1: 16
